  (text "LED CHAIN  (9x SK6812MINI-E, level-shifted from GPIO20)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 186.69 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f3ff4585-da3a-5ddd-9491-763de0fc6ecc"))
  (text "POWER  (JST battery input + BAT flying leads to the XIAO)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 224.79 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "089b0f11-47cc-5a0c-85c6-39d8c5a284d6"))
  (text "PASSIVES  (LED/encoder/shifter decoupling, bulk, VBAT sense divider)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 104.14 224.79 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9c421ef7-4781-59de-bd36-7d5ea12ad904"))
  (text "RGB power budget: 12mA/channel x 3 x 9 LEDs = 324mA at full white. Fed from VSYS, NOT +3V3 -- SK6812MINI-E's own datasheet specs VDD 3.7-5.5V, below what the 3.3V rail can supply. VSYS is the Li-ion cell/USB rail; it can sag below 3.7V well within normal discharge, so the LEDs may misbehave on a low battery even with brightness capped -- a limitation of the part choice, not a defect here." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.78 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0ac8d44b-2c66-53f4-bdea-92679fdc2a67"))
  (text "J2 (in PASSIVES) is the pad pair for the two flying leads soldered to the XIAO module's UNDERSIDE BAT+/BAT- pads. The XIAO sits on female headers and its battery terminals are on its bottom face, so no PCB pad can mate with them; without J2 the VSYS rail J1 feeds never reaches the module at all." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.78 248.92 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0a8b494e-fa05-5ff2-86bd-cec5a65efd55"))
  (rectangle (start 15.24 15.24) (end 149.86 105.41)
